# Backend Stack & Conventions (NestJS)

## Module Structure

Each domain feature is a NestJS module in `apps/api/src/modules/`:

```
modules/
├── rag/        # Ask questions, semantic search (RAG pipeline)
├── sources/    # Knowledge source management (GitHub, docs, files)
├── content/    # Team-curated content entries
└── auth/       # Authentication & authorization (JWT)
```

Each module follows the pattern: `module.ts`, `controller.ts`, `service.ts`, and `dto/` folder.

## DTOs & Validation

- Use `class-validator` decorators for input validation
- Use `class-transformer` for transformation
- DTOs live in `modules/<feature>/dto/` folder
- Use `!` definite assignment for DTO properties (they are populated by the validation pipe, not constructors)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export class AskQuestionDto {
  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  question!: string;  // note the ! — required for strict mode
}
```

## Swagger / OpenAPI

- **Every controller and endpoint must have Swagger decorators** — `@ApiTags`, `@ApiOperation`, `@ApiBearerAuth` (if auth required)
- DTOs should use `@ApiProperty` / `@ApiPropertyOptional`
- Docs auto-served at `http://localhost:4000/docs`

## Configuration

- Use `@nestjs/config` with `ConfigService` — never read `process.env` directly
- Env files resolve from both `apps/api/.env` and root `../../.env`

## API Conventions

- Global prefix: `/api/v1` (set in `main.ts`)
- CORS enabled for `http://localhost:3000`
- Global `ValidationPipe` with whitelist + transform enabled
